From 94a48626b96939428dc797cf2b03c90de1492f80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:30:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/38] TLS: GCC 16.2 model selection on all four targets;
 assembler, linker and unwind gaps

The TLS access model is max(default, -ftls-model floor, tls_model
attribute) over GD < LD < IE < LE, as GCC 16.2 decides it:

* executables: definitions in the image use LE, extern TLS uses IE;
* -fPIC: x86-64 and i686 use gnu2 descriptors (@TLSDESC/@TLSCALL),
  never IE/DF_STATIC_TLS, so a dlopen'ed 1 MiB TLS library loads;
  AArch64 uses :tlsdesc: plus .tlsdesccall; RISC-V uses la.tls.gd;
* i686 non-PIC extern TLS uses @INDNTPOFF, locals @NTPOFF.

Before this, non-PIC executables read extern __thread from a DSO via LE
(garbage), -fPIC objects carried TPOFF32 (every -shared link failed), and
the tls_model attribute was accepted but ignored.

Assemblers: i686 @INDNTPOFF -> R_386_TLS_IE as GAS emits it,
@TLSDESC/@TLSCALL; AArch64 :tlsdesc:/:tlsdesc_lo12:/.tlsdesccall/
:gottprel:/:gottprel_lo12:; RISC-V alignment, label-difference,
section-symbol and ULEB128 fixes.

Linkers: RISC-V and AArch64 .eh_frame_hdr/PT_GNU_EH_FRAME (exec and
shared), DT_RUNPATH, crt objects and default libraries for -shared,
linker scripts in -l lookup, a missing -lfoo is an error; lccc-ld refuses
LE relocations against DSO-defined TLS as GNU ld does.

Gates: check_tls_dynamic_witness, check_tls_model_option,
check_i686_tls_ie_relax, check_cfi_unwind, check_riscv_relax_layout,
check_builtin_dso_link. Ledger: engineering/FINDINGS-2026-10-20-s81-series.md
(TLS-*, ASM-*, RV-*, A64-*, I686-* rows).
