From afd8d1ebc25116cb1a669a3495789163fcea0dcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:30:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/38] x86/i686: TLS direct-load fold part 2, LEA width +
 composition, relay/frame fixes

TLS (part 2 of UP-TLS-FOLD-DEAD):
- One shared compute_omitted_tls_roots runs before the prologue
  (CodegenState::omitted_tls_roots); both x86-64 and i686 prologues deny
  omitted roots registers and slots, so allocation and emission agree by
  construction (fixes i686 `g` pushing %esi/%edi for never-written roots).
- Only default-address-space accesses qualify; segment-qualified accesses
  (`*(int __seg_fs *)&tls`) materialize the root (fixes reads of an
  unwritten register).
- i686 direct %gs: LE/IE loads and LE stores for omitted roots
  (byte-identical to GAS; `main` matches GCC 16.2).
- x86-64 LE `%fs:sym@TPOFF` load-op fusion via is_fusible_memory_operand
  (kill switch CCC_NO_SEG_OPERAND_FUSE); window alias safety unchanged.
- check_tls_model_option.sh: i686 and -Werror legs.

x86 LEA:
- MachInst Lea carries the operation width (S8/S16 -> S32): i32 x*3/5/9
  emit leal.
- Immediate-multiply text path: 64-bit address registers (32-bit address
  registers cost an addr32 0x67 prefix; the result is identical).
- fold_lea_add_into_lea (flags dead, width-matched).
- Move relays across self-addressed LEAs; leal reads only the low 32 bits.
- compose_displaced_relay; fold_lea_into_load composes displacements and
  lets the consumer write an address register (ModRM computed first;
  %rsp/stack ops/self-base excluded).
- fold_lea_into_memory_op: the redefining-consumer path requires exactly
  one source mention of the LEA destination (the one-slot splice turned
  `leaq -3(%rdi),%r10; leaq (%r10,%r10,4),%r10` into a stale-index
  `leaq -3(%rdi,%r10,4),%r10`; caught by vectorize_map_i32_scale_add).
- compose_self_scaled_lea: `lea d(%B),%T; lea d2(%T,%T,s),%D` ->
  `lea d(1+s)+d2(%B,%B,s),%D` (leaq->leaq mod 2^64; leaq/leal->leal mod
  2^32; leal->leaq refused; %rsp base, addr32, disp32 overflow refused).

Other:
- coalesce_copy_into_rmw: call-result relays through %r11.
