+/// [`is_plain_memory_operand`] plus the base-less Local-Exec TLS operand
+/// `%fs:sym@TPOFF[±N]` (`%gs:sym@NTPOFF[±N]` on i386): a fixed, register-free
+/// location the backend's TLS fold emits, which GCC 16.2 carries into the ALU
+/// op (`addl %fs:s@tpoff, %eax`). Only for parsers whose fusions re-emit the
+/// operand VERBATIM; it carries no `(…)` to rebase, so displacement-deriving
+/// passes (movbe pairing) keep the plain predicate. Alias safety is the
+/// window's: `accesses_memory` counts every `:`-bearing line as memory.
+fn is_fusible_memory_operand(op: &str) -> bool {
+    is_plain_memory_operand(op) || is_tls_absolute_operand(op)
+}
