From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:30:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/38] i686: GOT32X relaxation at ld 2.47 parity, GOT/GOTPC
 assembler gaps, five lccc-ld GOT bugs

Assembler (byte- and relocation-identical to GAS 2.47 --32; asm-diff
i686 688/688, x86-64 1434/1434):
- R_386_GOT32X exactly where GAS 2.47 emits it: movl loads (incl.
  base-less), call*/jmp*, testl reg/mem, ALU mem->reg, pushl (2.47; 2.44
  kept GOT32).  Stores, memory-destination ALU, leal, $x@GOT, narrow and
  imul forms keep R_386_GOT32 (relax_got32: a post-encode ModRM check).
- testl reg,mem / mem,reg forms (were "unsupported test operands").
- @GOT loads never take the moffs (A1) short form (ModRM 05, as GAS).
- `addl $_GLOBAL_OFFSET_TABLE_+[.-1b], %ebx`: R_386_GOTPC with A = P-1b
  (the writer's label-difference rule coerced it to PC32; unknown
  _GLOBAL_OFFSET_TABLE_ expressions are now a hard error).
- Numeric local labels inside expression immediates (`1b` in the GOTPC
  form escaped as an undefined symbol).
- Bare-symbol absolute operands for push/pop/not/neg/mul/div
  (`pushl sym` = ff 35, `popl sym` = 8f 05, `notl sym` = f7 15).

Linker (lccc-ld, non-PIE; conversions as ld 2.47 elf_i386_convert_load_reloc):
- GOT32X conversion: mov -> movl $x (C7), ALU -> 81 /op, test -> F7 /0,
  push -> 2E 68, call* -> 67 E8, jmp* -> E9 rel32 + 90.  Only with a zero
  in-place addend (the GOT32X addend offsets the SLOT); never for IFUNC,
  _DYNAMIC or undefined weak targets; SIB call forms left unconverted.
- Fixed: globals were never relaxed; locals got sym-GOT (a GOTOFF value
  in an absolute site); `static` symbols of two objects shared one slot
  (a name collision is now a hard error naming @GOTOFF as the remedy);
  base-less unconverted fields got slot-GOT instead of the absolute slot
  address (SIGSEGV for -fno-plt `call *f@GOT`); a nonzero addend would
  have converted wrongly.  The pre-fix lccc-ld segfaulted on the new
  gate's GAS-assembled objects; now runtime-correct with GAS or lccc
  objects under lccc-ld, bfd and lld alike.

Tests: tests/regression/check_i686_got32x_relax.sh (<0.2 s; runtime
matrix, converted-form census, collision refusal) in ci_local --fast and
CI; symgot.casefile groups for every form; unit tests for the GOT32X
decode table (incl. FF /0 /1, SIB, disp8, 0F map, nonzero addend),
base-less detection, GOTPC expression parsing and numeric-label rewrite.
