From e3a17aed0c9d12254a80f2a0e4abbe8e4810364c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:30:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/38] regalloc: phi-blocker rehoming, Phase 2c saved reuse,
 Phase 1 stickiness, save-set compaction

Callee-saved homing, measured with Callgrind at -O2
(engineering/FINDINGS-2026-10-20-homing.md):

* PhiBlockerRehome: a blocker in a loop phi's register is moved into an
  already-saved callee-saved register, or into a caller-saved one when it
  is caller-saved already and meets no call, so the latch copy leaves the
  loop. Coalesce-group members never move (CCC_NO_PHI_BLOCKER_REHOME).
* Phase 2c tier 1 competes for already-saved registers, seeded with their
  holders' bounds (the span-pressure valve is kept), before opening a
  fresh one (CCC_NO_PHASE2C_REUSE).
* Phase 1 prefers touched callee-saved registers over round-robin
  rotation (CCC_NO_CALLEE_STICKY). Not in the Phase 2c fresh tier: without
  weight-aware eviction, placement order picks the spill victim, and
  sticky placement spilled zstd's hot value (+4.0%).
* compact_callee_saved_homes folds a register's whole holder set into
  another saved register when every holder fits (CCC_NO_SAVE_SET_COMPACT).
  Prologue pushes over the benchmark programs: 336 -> 297.

Peephole: vector/FP -> GPR transfers (`vmovq %xmm,%rax`, `vpextr*`,
`cvt*2si`, ...) are pure writes of their GPR (adler32's phantom %rax
read); a 32-bit cmov zero-extends its destination even when not taken
(REDEXT-CMOV32-UPPER); `fold_setcc_test_cmov` respects retired families.

Tests: phi_coalesce_tests, save_set_compact_tests (4, 2 mutants caught),
prefer_touched (2), widened_copy_tracking_tests (3), volatile_reduce
costly_tls; mutation 7/7.
