From 1611d8df9b44a0e3cde7fae69b5221ed64e511bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:30:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/38] prefetch: GCC-exact __builtin_prefetch hints, i686 SSE
 gate, PRFCHW, scaled-index fold

Red-team of #887 (defects 14-17):
- i686 emitted SSE prefetcht* on the pre-SSE baseline (-m32, -march=i686,
  -mno-sse) where GCC emits nothing and the opcode is #UD. Gate on
  Driver::resolved_prefetch_sse (GCC ix86_prefetch_sse: SSE || PRFCHW).
- Payload kept write intent but dropped locality. PrefetchHint now encodes
  locality | write<<2; AArch64 uses GCC's pftype[rw&1][loc] (L3KEEP for
  locality 1, PST* keep their locality).
- Hint arguments: any integer constant expression (GCC), non-constant is an
  error, out-of-range warns and uses zero, rw=2 is a read hint.
- PRFCHW: -mprfchw/-mno-prfchw (sticky), measured -march table, native CPUID
  probe, __PRFCHW__; write hints become prefetchw.
- CCC_NO_PREFETCH read once by the driver and honoured by every backend.
- Shared x86/i686 mnemonic table; misplaced FMA doc comment restored.
- Peephole fold_scaled_index_temp_into_mem: the &a[i+K] software-prefetch
  idiom now addresses through one SIB operand (GCC shape).
