From 57b1f49d13594cf9e175b60a56c29d116ad227f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:30:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/38] Honour __attribute__((target("..."))) per function on
 x86

GCC compiles a function carrying target("bmi2") etc. with that ISA and
refuses to inline it into a caller lacking the features. LCCC parsed and
dropped the attribute, so zstd's *_bmi2 dispatch clones compiled to the
baseline ISA (0 BMI instructions vs GCC's 15-136 per clone).

- parser: target/__target__ -> FunctionAttributes.target
- IR: normalize_target_features -> IrFunction.target_features (sorted,
  deduplicated, lower-case)
- inliner: target_isa_allows_inline (callee features must be a subset of
  the caller's), matching GCC's can_inline_p for these features
- x86 backend: set_function_target_features scopes ScalarIsa
  {bmi1,bmi2,lzcnt,popcnt} per function; SHLX_MODE is thread-local
