 Phase 0 by recursion only

GCC inlines always_inline bodies unconditionally; failure is a hard
error, never a silent out-of-line call. LCCC refused any always_inline
callee above the 500-instruction/500-block relaxed tier and drained
clone-born sites with a flat counter (2x entry + 16), after which the
instruction-metered fallback passes (200 + 400) could not absorb big
templates. zstd lost every FORCE_INLINE_TEMPLATE specialisation:
ZSTD_compressBlock_opt_generic (803 IR insts), lazy_generic (22 callers),
doubleFast_dictMatchState_generic, HUF body_loop, ZSTD_decodeSequence.
Constant template arguments (optLevel, searchMethod, dictMode, unroll
flags) were never propagated; c-19 ran 1.95x GCC's instruction count.

- always_inline admission: only a resource guard (16384 insts / 4096
  blocks, >10x every real body seen) may refuse. The 500 tier still
  governs ordinary statics of section-attributed callers.
- Phase 0 spends its counter only on callees that lie on a cycle of the
  full direct call graph (iterative Tarjan, O(V+E)). Acyclic expansion
  terminates by itself; the full graph (not the always_inline subgraph)
  is a sound superset because later inlining only composes edges, and
  devirtualisation runs before the graph is built.
- PHASE0_CALLER_GUARD_INSTRUCTIONS (262144) bounds diamond-DAG fan-out.

Tests: SCC classification (self, mutual, 3-cycle, acyclic, declaration);
admission above the old cap and refusal above the guard; HUF-shaped
fan-out drained completely (fails with the flat counter). The joint
fixpoint test now reaches the second pass through a recursive template,
the only remaining way to get there.
