Register allocation / homing
- Frame-address producers that every user folds (alloca-rooted imm32
  offsets, and indexed folds the emitter re-forms against %rbp) no longer
  take a register or a stack home: dead callee saves across the -O2 corpus
  228 -> 97, instructions 201922 -> 190807, stack-operand instructions
  34234 -> 32202 (789 files, main -> series).
- [RA-HOMES] diagnostics live in regalloc.rs next to the decisions they
  explain.
- check: hot_web_callee_saved.c is an outcome gate (every pushed
  callee-saved register is used; no memory-destination ALU on N(%rsp)).

Correctness
- AArch64 BitTest with an immediate index >= the operand width emitted an
  unencodable `lsr w0, w1, #40` (rejected by every assembler; series and
  main). The IR now documents the index as taken modulo the width -- what
  x86 BT, AArch64 LSRV and RISC-V SRL/SRLW all do -- and AArch64 emits one
  `ubfx #(i mod W), #1` for every immediate (31/63 were `lsr; and`).
  Constant folding states the same rule with wrapping_shr instead of
  relying on the build profile's shift masking.
- check_arm_codegen_assembles.sh: a non-preprocessor compile failure of an
  arm_*.c regression is FAIL, not a silent "preprocessor skip".
- check_vectorize_round_maps.sh: default -O3 keeps errno-setting sqrt
  calls (GCC 16.2 / Clang 23.1.3 agree); -fno-math-errno vectorizes.

