From d4b440f3ed263086e1fcf945953f5d2914ee1268 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:21:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/38] x86 select: live flags always consumed in place;
 FP-select cmov mapping total

- A select whose condition's flags are live (fused integer Cmp, the
  FP-select fallback's ucomis, a replayed compare) never materialized the
  boolean. CCC_NO_INPLACE_SELECT was checked first and sent it down the
  materialized path, which tested a stale home: 99 of 324 checks of the
  new regression took the wrong arm at -O2/-O3. The switch now only turns
  off the optional in-place test of a materialized condition.
- emit_fp_cmp_boolean returns the cmov condition its ucomis left live
  (`a`/`ae`) instead of parking a jcc string in the shared pending_fp_cmp
  slot. The select's match loses its silent `(None, Some(_)) => "ne"` arm:
  the CondBranch fusion's two-flag pair sentinels cannot reach a cmov by
  construction (previously only by the prologue's CondBranch-only gate).
  Corrects the stale comment claiming FP Eq/Ne never fuse.

Output-neutral by default: every tests/regression/*.c compiles to
byte-identical assembly (the only differences were the PGO PID, fixed
separately).

Test: select_live_flags_no_inplace_knob.c (+ .env CCC_NO_INPLACE_SELECT=1):
integer/unsigned/FP relational (NaN, signed zeros, infinities), FP Eq/Ne,
replayed compare; self-checking and == GCC 16.2 at O0..O3/Os with and
without the switch. Before: FAIL at -O2/-O3.
