From 7738c39e76ecd1558892270030f9dd26a7a5303c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:21:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/38] pgo: reproducible -fprofile-generate output (no
 compiler PID in names)

The directory-mode profile file (`lccc-<hash>-<unit>-<pid>.profraw`) and
the dump helper (`__lccc_pgo_dump_<uid>_<pid>`) embedded the compiler's
process ID, so two identical compiles produced different assembly and
objects: no reproducible builds, no build-cache hits.
Neither suffix bought anything. The helper has internal linkage and is
registered in its own unit's .fini_array (its sibling
`__lccc_pgo_lookup_<uid>` never had a suffix). Every training process
appends to the profile under flock, and the loader merges records by
function key and CFG hash (a re-instrumented unit's records stay apart
under `#cfg<hash>`), so one file per unit is what the writer was built
for; its record order is now chronological instead of PID-sorted.
check_codegen_refactor_identity.py keeps canonicalizing the old form for
comparisons against older baselines.

Tests: profile_output_path_is_a_pure_function_of_the_unit (unit);
check_pgo_io.py directory mode: identical .s and .o across two compiles,
one profile file appended by two runs with exactly doubled counters, and
-fprofile-use=DIR ingests it (75 PASS; before: FAIL "instrumented assembly
differs between identical compiles").
