From de0c2d8d01747a8ab6458100b69c69b942661cc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:44:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/38] peephole liveness: memoise line effects, flat successor
 edges

Callgrind on lccc compiling zstd 1.5.7 huf_compress.c at -O2 put 49% of all
instructions in FileLiveness::analyse_function. The function memo rarely
hits while passes edit the function: 12,810 real solves out of ~13,650
calls. Each solve re-derived every line's register effect from its text:
straight_effect ran 6.88M times at ~1,820 Ir, a quarter of the compile, in
src_mentions_family's substring searches, is_read_modify_write, the
mnemonic prefix scan and the implicit-operand oracle. Each solve also
allocated a Vec of successors per line.

straight_effect is a pure function of the trimmed text, `kind` (which
carries the destination get_dest_reg reports) and `reg_refs`. A per-thread
memo now keys on exactly those three and compares them for equality on a
hit, so a hit is the uncached answer by construction, with no hash-collision
argument. A text re-typed by a pass without an edit recomputes and replaces
its entry. The table is bounded at 32K entries and cleared, not frozen,
when full.

classify now appends successors to one flat buffer, with a (first, past)
range per line, instead of returning a Vec: one buffer per solve instead of
an allocation and a free per line. The edge order and the ret fallback
(an empty range reads ret_live) are unchanged.

huf_compress.c: 49.99G -> 34.73G Ir (-30.5%); analyse_function 24.58G ->
9.30G. The assembly is byte-identical. Tests: the memo answers like the
uncached derivation on a line set covering every branch, the second round
is served from the memo (hit counter), and the key covers `kind` and
`reg_refs` (re-typing and widening recompute; restoring answers the
original).
