From b4729879365123940b6ab5b0809e52d8de7c6c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:21:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/38] x86 emitter: hand isel a freshness view, not a
 per-instruction map copy

fresh_ra_for_isel copied every fresh entry of the function's assignment
map into a new FxHashMap for each lowered instruction. That is
O(function) per instruction: 7,852 lowerings over thousands of homes on
zstd huf_compress.c cost 2.15 G Ir, 9% of the compile, while a lowering
reads a handful of entries.

isel now takes &dyn HomeMap: get / contains_key / any_home. FreshHomes
borrows the emitter and applies the same freshness filter per lookup.
The emitter is borrowed for the whole lowering (machinst_buf is moved
out and back), so no home can change between the old copy and the new
lookups. The answers are identical by construction, including
xmm_scratch_unsafe's whole-map question, which any_home answers over the
same filtered set. Plain maps implement the trait, so tests and the
other callers are unchanged. dyn rather than generics keeps one copy of
the 3,200-line isel.

The sign-extension fixup after a typed S32 lowering read the old copy
after the lowering. Only machinst_buf changes in between, so it queries
the view.
