From 36c0a0e3d1092392285bcbb35fd5b4c7de273ac6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:19:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/38] simplify: fold truncations of two-register packs;
 exact-width carrier

`packed_range_source` walks or/shl/lshr/ashr/and/casts (depth 12) to the
value that supplies a truncation's bit range, so `trunc(lshr(or(zext lo,
shl(zext hi, 64)), 64))` becomes `hi` with no I128 traffic. Never W = 128
on 32-bit targets, never returns a 128-bit source; narrow constants'
upper bits are trusted only when non-negative (`const_range_is`: x86
zero-extends narrow constants into RDX while imm32 sign-extends).
cast_narrow refuses trunc-of-trunc onto I128; cast chains compare
same-width sign variants as the same bits.

`unpack_two_reg_return` stores the high eightbyte at exact width
(U8/U16/U32/I64) and rounds odd-remainder allocas to 16: the old I64
store at offset 8 of a 12-byte object wrote out of bounds.
Regression test two_reg_return_carrier.c (i686-guarded __int128 part).
